    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NrsjZR67sYLkLtKqkMhftf)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-notes`: removed the `consult-notes` package. `C-c w d f` (notebook) stays and `C-c w d g` now runs `sp-search-in-notes` (ripgrep over the notes), set with plain `global-set-key`.\n- `sp-keys`: `n s` (notes prefix) and the `n` key of the search map now call `sp-search-in-notes` instead of `consult-notes-search-in-all-notes`.\n- `sp-search`: removed the `c` and `C` consult-notes entries from the notes menu (`n` and `v` stay).\n- Docs updated (`sp-notes.org`, `sp-keys.org`, `sp-search-browsing-trails.org`, `load-order.org`, README row).\n\n## Not changed\n- The third-party clone under `cloned/consult-omni` has a `consult-notes` source; it loads the package with `(require ... nil t)`, so it is skipped without it.\n- The theme faces for `consult-notes-*` in `lambda-themes.el` are inert.\n\n## Testing\n- Docs tangle to the committed `.el` (ignoring whitespace); the 17 `sp-notes` ERT tests pass in batch Emacs 29.3.\n- /untested/ in the real Emacs (key bindings, search menu).\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9hnWskPJso94gsTkL)_",
